3331
02:55:23,530 --> 02:55:44,900
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: Bong Go, I'll make a brief presentation to introduce the Games and Amusements Board to the body. The Games and Amusements Board is the agency in charge of regulating and supervising professional sports in the Philippines. Oftentimes, it is mistaken for its bigger cousin, which is called the Philippine Sports Commission.

3332
02:55:44,920 --> 02:55:55,440
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: The Games and Amusements Board currently supervises a total of 17 non-contact sports and 6 contact sports.

3333
02:55:56,560 --> 02:56:04,760
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: The Games and Amusements Board, in the course of supervising and regulating professional sports, collects regulatory fees.

3334
02:56:05,820 --> 02:56:10,560
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: In 2025, it collected a total of 30 million pesos.

3335
02:56:10,560 --> 02:56:14,560
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: Aside from regulating and supervising professional sports,

3336
02:56:14,920 --> 02:56:23,900
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: the Games and Amusements Board is also in charge of the betting aspect of horse racing and the licensing of international derbies.

3337
02:56:24,680 --> 02:56:32,760
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: It also undertakes law enforcement operations in coordination with the Philippine National Police and the National Bureau of Investigation.

3338
02:56:33,760 --> 02:56:40,920
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: In 2025, the GAMS operations led to the arrest of a total of 194 persons,

3339
