3398
02:59:14,800 --> 02:59:24,700
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: At present, Senator Bong, we are

3399
02:59:24,700 --> 02:59:38,180
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: Assured that before they are penalized or before they get disciplined, they'll be afforded their full right to due process of law

3400
02:59:38,180 --> 02:59:54,700
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: About some medical insurance, yung gabho ba require professional sports promoters, leagues, and organizers to provide medical insurance or accident coverage to participating athletes?

3401
02:59:57,560 --> 03:00:00,020
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: Yes, Senator. For example,

3402
03:00:00,000 --> 03:00:11,580
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: For example, for motorsports, the Games and Amusements Board requires that before we license a player, he must first submit an insurance coverage.

3403
03:00:11,580 --> 03:00:30,660
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: But this requirement is meeting with a lot of difficulties because our insurance companies generally do not cover risks involving professional athletes, especially on sports that are considered risky, like motorsports and boxing.

3404
03:00:33,520 --> 03:00:37,080
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: Wala namang reklamo itong mga professional athletes natin.

3405
03:00:37,900 --> 03:00:41,260
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: Our professional athletes guaranteed timely payouts.

3406
03:00:41,580 --> 03:00:50,280
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: Payment of their salaries, yung kanilang fight purses, yung prices, and other contractual compensation.

3407
03:00:51,220 --> 03:00:57,340
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: So far, Senator, we haven't received this year any complaint for non-payment of salaries.

3408
03:00:57,640 --> 03:01:09,140
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: Now, last year, there were complaints involving basketball players, but those complaints were withdrawn and it appears to us that they were addressed by their teams.

3409
03:01:10,420 --> 03:01:11,420
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: A question.

3410
03:01:11,580 --> 03:01:21,140
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Chairman Pato, itong sa volleyball, basketball, meron tayong PBA, sanctioned by the GAB.

3411
03:01:22,300 --> 03:01:27,800
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Sa volleyball naman, we have this Philippine Volleyball League, sa Women's.

3412
03:01:27,800 --> 03:01:28,540
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: Premier Volleyball League.

3413
03:01:28,640 --> 03:01:31,600
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Premier Volleyball League. Sa inyo po yun?

3414
03:01:32,140 --> 03:01:33,200
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: Yes, Senator Bong.

3415
03:01:33,500 --> 03:01:35,560
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Sa inyo sila kumukuha ng lisensya?

3416
03:01:35,880 --> 03:01:36,500
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: Yes, Senator Bong.

3417
03:01:36,500 --> 03:01:40,500
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Sanction nyo po sila during games, nandiyo dyan kayo, you attend, you witness.

3418
03:01:41,580 --> 03:01:42,520
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: Yes, Senator Bong.

3419
03:01:43,520 --> 03:01:49,380
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: How about this sa men's volleyball? Kasi wala silang professional.

3420
03:01:49,380 --> 03:02:10,380
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: So ano pwedeng ma-explain nyo po sa ating mga kababayan, including Chairman Pato, ano ho bang pinakaiba na ngayon sa women's volleyball with the men's since walang professional yung men's.

3421
03:02:10,380 --> 03:02:21,900
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: And then yung kanilang mga matatanggap sa inyo, sa PSC, na tulong since they are now professionals.

3422
03:02:24,220 --> 03:02:25,840
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: Yes, Senator Bong.

3423
03:02:26,480 --> 03:02:31,160
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: The PSC and the Games and Amusements Board have a joint resolution.

3424
03:02:31,840 --> 03:02:39,080
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: In that resolution, we demarcate the line between professionals as against non-professionals.

3425
03:02:39,080 --> 03:03:01,920
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: Now, the general definition of a professional is one who participates in a sporting event, and in that participation he's paid a sum of money, either a salary or as a prize. Now, if you're paid a sum of money for participating in a sporting event

3426
03:03:01,920 --> 03:03:02,940
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: as a professional.

3427
03:03:04,880 --> 03:03:09,900
GAB Chairperson Atty. Francisco J. Rivera: That's the definition of who constitutes a professional athlete.

3428
03:03:09,900 --> 03:03:36,580
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: So wala na sa PSC, wala na silang natatanggap sa na-allowances and benefits from PSC since they are now nasa Pro League na po sila, kahit na nag-represent sila sa country. Ano yung matatanggap pa rin nila sa inyo sa PSC since they are representing the country even though they are professionals?

3429
03:03:36,580 --> 03:04:06,560
PSC OIC Executive Director Atty. Guillermo B. Iroy Jr.: Good afternoon, Chairman. Professional players, when they represent the country in international competition through the National Sports Association, are still able to receive what amateur athletes get, for example free airfare, accommodation, allowances, and training requirements, just like the volleyball players when they participated in the Southeast Asian Games.

3430
03:04:06,580 --> 03:04:29,700
PSC OIC Executive Director Atty. Guillermo B. Iroy Jr.: In the Pro League, they requested, this is volleyball, sir, they requested for an allowance. The board approved. In fact, at the time, the volleyball is under POC. So for as long as the professional player, whatever sports they are, they will be endorsed by the National Sports Federation to represent the country in international competition.

3431
03:04:29,700 --> 03:04:36,560
PSC OIC Executive Director Atty. Guillermo B. Iroy Jr.: They can receive allowances and other expenses that required for the team.

3432
03:04:36,580 --> 03:04:53,980
PSC OIC Executive Director Atty. Guillermo B. Iroy Jr.: To participate in the international competition. Especially next year, if you, for the information of the chair, I think of all the sports now, only wrestling has no professional competition.

3433
03:04:54,540 --> 03:05:06,520
PSC OIC Executive Director Atty. Guillermo B. Iroy Jr.: That is the only remaining sports that is amateur in nature. But the rest of the sports from athletics up to in PAC, even boobinam, they have professional sports already.

3434
03:05:06,580 --> 03:05:17,040
PSC OIC Executive Director Atty. Guillermo B. Iroy Jr.: So right now, the only thing that we cannot fund is when they represent the club. But if they represent the country, the PSC can still fund them.

3435
03:05:17,240 --> 03:05:19,700
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Wala na silang regular monthly allowances no more?

3436
03:05:20,460 --> 03:05:29,800
PSC OIC Executive Director Atty. Guillermo B. Iroy Jr.: Wala silang monthly allowances, sir, because for example, the volleyball women, they were not endorsed to us by the Federation for allowances.

3437
03:05:30,840 --> 03:05:36,440
PSC OIC Executive Director Atty. Guillermo B. Iroy Jr.: However, if they represent the country, they are endorsed for allowances at the same time.

3438
03:05:36,580 --> 03:05:37,040
PSC OIC Executive Director Atty. Guillermo B. Iroy Jr.: We approve.

3439
03:05:37,340 --> 03:05:39,640
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: So yung nag-compete sila sa Asian Games, meron?

3440
03:05:39,800 --> 03:05:40,380
PSC OIC Executive Director Atty. Guillermo B. Iroy Jr.: Meron, sir.

3441
03:05:41,000 --> 03:05:43,520
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Anong duration lang po ang pano nila?

3442
03:05:43,880 --> 03:05:54,480
PSC OIC Executive Director Atty. Guillermo B. Iroy Jr.: Depende sa kanilang, for example, they go into camp for two weeks, the NEC requested, it will be approved for as long as it related to the international competition.

3443
03:05:55,680 --> 03:05:57,520
PSC OIC Executive Director Atty. Guillermo B. Iroy Jr.: For example, Asian Games.

3444
03:05:57,520 --> 03:06:06,520
PSC OIC Executive Director Atty. Guillermo B. Iroy Jr.: I think one of the reason this volleyball issue came up because every time they go to international competition, they have at least one month or two.

3445
03:06:06,580 --> 03:06:08,200
PSC OIC Executive Director Atty. Guillermo B. Iroy Jr.: Two weeks training camp.

3446
03:06:08,740 --> 03:06:13,220
PSC OIC Executive Director Atty. Guillermo B. Iroy Jr.: And I think it was not endorsed to us by the Federation at that time.

3447
03:06:13,300 --> 03:06:15,260
